<%# chat-scroll: after this tab's own composer submit (turbo:submit-end bubbles
    up from the form), the next post appended to the log below is scrolled into
    view — see chat_scroll_controller.js for why broadcasts must not arm it. %>
<%# data-chat-id: the frame says which thread it is showing. Plain self-
    description, and the assistant panel depends on it: its header lives in a
    data-turbo-permanent node, so the server can never re-render it and it has no
    other way of learning which thread the frame ended up holding (the "Frühere
    Verläufe" button needs exactly that). Deliberately on the frame rather than a
    wrapper — a wrapper here, even display:contents, breaks the panel's flex
    column (measured: the transcript stops scrolling in its own container). %>
<turbo-frame id="<%= frame_id %>" data-chat-id="<%= @chat.id %>" data-controller="chat-scroll" data-action="turbo:submit-end->chat-scroll#arm">
  <%# persisted? guard: turbo_stream_from raises on a record without a Global ID. No
      caller renders an unsaved chat since S4-T1 (chats/show finds a persisted one, the
      assistant panel gates on persisted? itself and shows the bare composer otherwise),
      so this is a fail-soft for a future empty-state render, not a path walked today. %>
  <%= turbo_stream_from chatposts_stream_name if @chat.persisted? %>
  <%# a1 (Plan §6): the asker also listens on their own stream for the live token deltas;
      the shared stream above carries the placeholder + the completion page-refresh. %>
  <%= turbo_stream_from viewer_stream if @current_user && @chat.persisted? %>

  <%# hover-reveal sits on the LOG, not on the message: "at most one message
      shows its actions" is a rule about all of them together, and only the list
      can hold it. This is also the element that scrolls inside the assistant
      panel, which the controller listens to -- scrolling moves rows under a
      pointer that never moved. See hover_reveal_controller.js. %>
  <div id="<%= chatposts_frame_id %>" role="log" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="false" data-chat-scroll-target="log" data-controller="hover-reveal">
    <% @chat.chatposts.each do |chatpost| %>
      <%= render message_for(chatpost) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if can_write? && chat_available? %>
    <%# The writing zone, read top to bottom in the order the question is asked:
        what the assistant is pointed AT, then the field, then how the answer
        should be written.

        WHAT it looks at moved above the field on 27.08.2026. Below it, at the
        bottom edge of a panel, under the style row and the transparency line,
        it was where nobody looked -- and it is the one setting you want to
        check BEFORE typing, because it decides what the question can even
        reach. The style row stayed below: it describes the answer, and it is
        the setting you leave alone for weeks at a time. %>
    <%# The offer of the page you just navigated to, directly above the row that
        shows the reference it would set. Panel only -- see #panel?. %>
    <% if panel? %>
      <%= render context_offer %>
    <% end %>
    <%# Reference and scope. Both chips render as `contents`, so their groups sit
        in this flex row instead of stacking rows with different spacing.
        Start-aligned, not end-aligned as it was under the field: it now reads as
        a caption of the field below it, and a caption starts where the text
        starts. flex-wrap for the 380px panel. %>
    <%# chat-context-row / chat-style-row: named so the arrangement can be MEASURED
        (spec/system/assistant_panel_layout_spec.rb). Both rows are flex parents of
        chips that render as `contents`, so the chips themselves have no geometry
        of their own -- these wrappers are the only things a bounding box can be
        taken of. No CSS hangs off either name. %>
    <div class="chat-context-row flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 mb-1">
      <%= render scope_row %>
    </div>
    <%= render composer %>
    <%# Answer-style selects, directly under the field they configure.
        turbo_stream-replaced by their DOM class after a change (target lives
        outside the chatposts log). Only rendered alongside the composer —
        without a writing affordance there is nothing to configure. justify-end
        + flex-wrap as before: quiet at the right edge, wrapping on a narrow
        panel rather than squeezing. %>
    <div class="chat-style-row mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-x-5 gap-y-2">
      <%= render style_control %>
    </div>
    <%# The AI transparency notice moved to the page footer area — the show
        views render TransparencyNoticeComponent below the chat card. %>
  <% elsif can_write? %>
    <%# No route for a message from here — no composer, say why instead. R4 widened
        this branch: it used to mean "org has not activated AI", it now covers every
        reason :chat can be unavailable for (a missing credential, a provider that
        cannot chat). explain_opt_in: true because this surface has ALWAYS spoken about
        the opt-in — for :ai_disabled the sentence is unchanged, word for word.
        Wrapped in the SAME turbo frame the composer uses: a stale-tab submit gets a
        302 from the controller guard, Turbo follows it INSIDE the form's frame, and
        without a matching frame id in the response the frame would error with
        "content missing" and swallow the alert. With it, the composer swaps to this
        notice — the user sees why sending stopped working. %>
    <%= turbo_frame_tag @chat.chatpost_form_dom_id do %>
      <%= render Neo::Ai::UnavailableHintComponent.new(
            availability: chat_availability, organisation: @current_organisation,
            variant: :warning, explain_opt_in: true, classes: 'mt-4') %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <%# D5 info: neutral notice → border-2 border-stroke, cobalt-50, icon, no shadow (embedded). %>
    <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-cobalt-50 border-2 border-stroke rounded text-sm text-gray-800 flex items-start gap-2">
      <i class="bi bi-info-circle text-cobalt-700 mt-0.5"></i>
      <span><%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.read_only') %></span>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</turbo-frame>
